{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a144f936-6dd5-49d3-b123-cd91826b0d23","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have completed the `lab-02-extensibility` implementation and committed the changes to the `aos/writer-part-0-1` branch. \n\nHere is a summary of the work:\n1.  **Exokernel Analogy**: Created `userfaultfd_demo.c`, a C program that leverages Linux's `userfaultfd` to safely manage page faults from user space. It registers a memory region and spawns a background thread that successfully intercepts memory access, mapping the page with `UFFDIO_COPY`.\n2.  **SPIN Analogy**: Created `trace_exec.sh`, a one-liner `bpftrace` script that dynamically hooks into the kernel's `sys_enter_execve` tracepoint to log execution events, demonstrating safe, verified kernel extensibility.\n3.  **Lab Structure**: Authored the `Makefile` ensuring `make test` runs both demonstrations natively within the nested Ubuntu VM using `sudo`. Also configured `.gitignore`.\n4.  **Documentation**: Updated `README.md` to `status: solid`, preserving seed frontmatter. Added execution instructions, conceptual mapping to L02b and L02c, expected outputs, three experiments with predictions, and three detailed Q\u0026A folds.\n5.  **Verification**: Evaluated the lab end-to-end within the Lima VM via `run-in-vm.sh \u003clab-dir\u003e test`. Captured the output into `expected-output.txt` using `run-in-vm.sh \u003clab-dir\u003e capture`. \n6.  **Report**: Wrote a final summary of steps and verifications to the requested crew report path.\n","duration_seconds":243.936216,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":195501,"output_tokens":17284,"thinking_tokens":6930,"cache_read_tokens":1685737,"total_tokens":212785}}}
